  {
   "id": "bb-307-atr",
   "h": "Red Eye — Atraumatic",
   "html": "<div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"b307a\"></div><div class=\"pearl\"><p><b>Clinical Pearl:</b></p><ul><li>Orbital cellulitis can present with pain on EOM and orbital signs of involvement</li></ul></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "bb-307-tr",
   "h": "Red Eye — Traumatic",
   "html": "<div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"b307b\"></div><p><small>** Urgent lateral canthotomy (Orbital Apex Injury/ Retrobulbar Fracture)</small></p><div class=\"pearl\"><p><b>Clinical Pearls:</b></p><ul><li>With chemical burns, it is important to determine if the burn was caused by acid or worse, alkali.</li><li>With a globe-penetrating injury, call ophthalmology, shield the eye, and do not touch the eye.</li></ul></div>"
  }
 ],
